--- !u!114 &46078117
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 46078114}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "This morning I decided: that's it, enough being a scrawny weakling. I
    looked in the mirror\u2014and for real, I\u2019m just a lifeless mannequin. I
    thought maybe if I bulk up a bit, join that basement gym or at least start doing
    push-ups at home, then she... well, maybe she\u2019d at least stop looking right
    through me.\r\nI went outside, planning to jog around the building, when this
    junkie from the first floor intercepted me\u2014that bald guy with the permanently
    bloodshot eyes. He crept up, looking over his shoulder every second. He was holding
    some newspaper. But that was bullshit. HE HAD A CONSOLE. CAN YOU BELIEVE IT?
    A CONSOLE!!! He wanted to sell it to me.\r\nAt first, I was gonna tell him to
    fuck off\u2014what money do I have? I\u2019ve only got a tenner in my pocket
    for a snack. But then I remembered the guys at school yapping about the Sony,
    how they stay up all night gaming. Some kind of wild curiosity hit me. Or was
    it envy? I told him to wait, and I ran back home to figure out where to get the
    cash. The gym can wait; I\u2019d look like a loser in there anyway. But a console?
    That\u2019s the real deal.\r\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
