--- !u!114 &1663446751
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1663446748}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Woke up to two different radios blasting at full volume inside my skull.
    The Principal\u2019s cold voice is hammering into my brain: 'Get up. Get dressed.
    April sixteenth. The Plan. The Routine.' But from the other side, right at the
    back of my head, the TV-guy starts braying ironically, turning every one of her
    words into a circus march.\r\n\r\nI tried to write down the date, like always,
    but my hand just froze on the paper. I wrote '16,' and then... a void. I look
    at the word 'April' in my head, and it\u2019s dissolving like wet newspaper.
    The letters 'A' and 'P' are warping, sprouting roots, turning into those same
    ironic mugs, smirking at me from the margins. I tried to rub them out, but they
    bleed right through my fingers. The Principal screams: 'Systematize!' while Chaos
    whispers: 'Just scribble over the whole damn thing.' It\u2019s not a balance;
    it\u2019s like being torn apart by two tractors pulling in opposite directions.
    The house is silent, but my head is buzzing like I\u2019ve shoved my ear into
    a transformer vault. The letters are dying. All that\u2019s left are these snarling
    faces.\r\n\r\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 45ae1b20a8af0b947bf46692f07a66b7, type: 2}
